"""
aa-sync -- materialise and load the selected subset of apparmor.d profiles.

Profiles ship read-only under <share> (default /usr/share/apparmor.d); aa-sync
selects a subset per /etc/apparmor/aa-sync.conf and owns the loaded set under
<state> (default /var/lib/apparmor.d): active/ is the loaded set, next/ is
staging swapped atomically into active/, manifest.json records the last apply.

Selection gates: stability (stable|testing|disabled, config picks which deploy)
and mode (no|used|group|all; "used" keeps profiles whose attached binary
exists). include globs force on, exclude globs force off (exclude wins).

<share>/index.json (built by `aa-sync index`) carries per-profile name(s),
attachment(s), stability and group(s). With it, "used"/group selection and drift
need no parsing; it is REQUIRED for mode=used on libs predating
apparmor.regex.resolve_variables (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04). Without it aa-sync parses
the share tree instead (stability.json is then required), group mode is
unavailable, and drift is basename-based.
"""

